# Line endings are decided here, not by each contributor's core.autocrlf.
#
# The index was all-LF before this file existed, but only because the development machine
# happens to have core.autocrlf=true. The Windows default when git is installed without the
# recommended option is false, which commits CRLF — and a shell launcher committed that way
# fails on Linux with `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, a message that points nowhere near the
# cause. `scripts/check-tracked-file-modes.mjs` holds the index to what this file says.
#
# The order matters: later rules win, so demo.gif has to come after the catch-all.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.excalidraw text eol=lf

demo.gif binary
